WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.942
What is it like to be a horse?

2
00:00:05.943 --> 00:00:13.108
I can tell you because I've been one all my life. And what a life it has been!

3
00:00:13.109 --> 00:00:18.564
The first thing I remember is the field where I was born.

4
00:00:18.565 --> 00:00:23.550
It had plenty of grass, a pond, and trees for shade.

5
00:00:23.551 --> 00:00:27.202
There was a shed at one end where we could stand when it was cold.

6
00:00:27.203 --> 00:00:34.512
Outside the fence lay more fields, a stream, and our master's house.

7
00:00:34.513 --> 00:00:40.487
My mother's name was Duchess, and she was a favorite of the master because of her sweet nature.

8
00:00:40.488 --> 00:00:46.103
Whenever she saw him, she would neigh and trot over to greet him.

9
00:00:46.104 --> 00:00:49.537
There were other mares and foals in the field as well.

10
00:00:49.538 --> 00:00:53.103
I ran and played with the other males.

11
00:00:53.104 --> 00:00:56.275
These colts were all older and bigger than me.

12
00:00:56.276 --> 00:01:01.293
Sometimes their play turned rough, with lots of kicking and biting.

13
00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:06.217
One day my mother called me away from them.

14
00:01:06.218 --> 00:01:10.618
"I hope you will grow up gentle and kind," she told me.

15
00:01:10.619 --> 00:01:14.269
"I do not want you to bite or kick, even in play.

16
00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:19.128
You should always be good, and do your work as well as you can."

17
00:01:19.129 --> 00:01:21.823
I never forgot this advice from my mother.

18
00:01:21.824 --> 00:01:24.466
Our master's name was Farmer Grey.

19
00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:28.217
He always had kind words and pats for all the horses.

20
00:01:28.218 --> 00:01:31.343
He was kind and fair to his workers as well.

21
00:01:31.344 --> 00:01:35.537
One of those workers was a boy named Dick.

22
00:01:35.538 --> 00:01:40.896
Sometimes, after Dick finished his work, he came into our field to pick berries.

23
00:01:40.897 --> 00:01:44.227
And sometimes that wasn't the only thing he did.

24
00:01:44.228 --> 00:01:47.386
"Hey, you!" he yelled at us one day.

25
00:01:47.387 --> 00:01:50.626
I was grazing nearby with the other colts.

26
00:01:50.627 --> 00:01:54.070
We all looked up at the sound of his voice.

27
00:01:54.071 --> 00:01:57.076
One of the bigger colts took a step toward him.

28
00:01:57.077 --> 00:02:02.184
I could tell the colt was hoping for a treat like the ones Farmer Grey often brought us.

29
00:02:02.185 --> 00:02:08.168
"Go on!" Dick shouted. "I want to see you run!"

30
00:02:08.169 --> 00:02:13.428
Then he threw a stick at the big colt! It hit him hard on the chest.

31
00:02:13.429 --> 00:02:19.361
The colt was so surprised that he snorted, whirled around, and kicked up his heels.

32
00:02:19.362 --> 00:02:24.512
Then he galloped off toward the mares, who were grazing at the other end of the field.

33
00:02:24.513 --> 00:02:30.293
That made the rest of us run too. Behind us I heard Dick laughing loudly.

34
00:02:30.294 --> 00:02:36.092
After that Dick often hurled sticks and stones at us to make us run.

35
00:02:36.093 --> 00:02:41.144
Once we understood his game, we stayed far enough away so he couldn't hit us.

36
00:02:41.145 --> 00:02:44.793
But once in a while a stone would hit me, and it hurt.

37
00:02:44.794 --> 00:02:47.733
None of us liked that boy very much.

38
00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:50.890
One day Dick began his game as usual.

39
00:02:50.891 --> 00:02:54.315
But he didn't know that Farmer Grey was in the next field.

40
00:02:54.316 --> 00:03:00.205
When our master saw what was going on, he rushed over and grabbed Dick by the arm.

41
00:03:00.206 --> 00:03:03.811
"Bad boy!" he scolded Dick sternly.

42
00:03:03.812 --> 00:03:07.567
"I can tell this is not the first time you've chased the colts.

43
00:03:07.568 --> 00:03:11.120
But it will be the last time. You're fired!"

44
00:03:11.121 --> 00:03:13.684
That was the last time we saw Dick.

45
00:03:13.685 --> 00:03:18.140
Other than Dick's visits, most of our days were quiet and pleasant.

46
00:03:18.141 --> 00:03:23.026
Yet there was one other incident that I have never forgotten.

47
00:03:23.027 --> 00:03:26.212
I was grazing in the field with the other colts.

48
00:03:26.213 --> 00:03:29.784
We all looked up when we heard dogs howling in the distance.

49
00:03:29.785 --> 00:03:32.832
The oldest colt pricked his ears and listened.

50
00:03:32.833 --> 00:03:37.883
"Those are the hounds!" he said, cantering over to the fence.

51
00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:41.381
The rest of us followed.

52
00:03:41.382 --> 00:03:45.787
"What's happening?" I asked my mother, who stood there, looking out.

53
00:03:45.788 --> 00:03:48.635
"It's the hunt," she told me.

54
00:03:48.636 --> 00:03:52.626
"Humans sometimes chase rabbits and foxes on horseback.

55
00:03:52.627 --> 00:03:56.082
The hounds help them follow the trail."

56
00:03:56.083 --> 00:03:59.110
We all watched as the hunters came into sight.

57
00:03:59.111 --> 00:04:03.529
The hounds came first, racing after a speedy rabbit.

58
00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:06.071
Next came a group of riders.

59
00:04:06.072 --> 00:04:09.854
The rabbit scampered down the hill and leaped across the stream.

60
00:04:09.855 --> 00:04:12.269
The hounds followed.

61
00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:15.314
Most of the horses jumped the stream easily.

62
00:04:15.315 --> 00:04:18.949
But one slipped on the grass and fell down.

63
00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:23.018
His rider, a handsome young man, was flung off.

64
00:04:23.019 --> 00:04:26.274
He landed hard and lay still on the grass.

65
00:04:26.275 --> 00:04:28.868
The others returned to check on him.

66
00:04:28.869 --> 00:04:34.431
But he never got up, and finally they carried him away.

67
00:04:34.432 --> 00:04:38.066
Later we heard that the fallen rider was George Gordon.

68
00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:42.473
He was the only son of Squire Gordon, the richest man in the area.

69
00:04:42.474 --> 00:04:46.173
George had broken his neck and died in the fall.

70
00:04:46.174 --> 00:04:49.815
When my mother heard the news, she looked sad.

71
00:04:49.816 --> 00:04:55.432
"I don't understand why people are so interested in hunting," she said.

72
00:04:55.433 --> 00:04:57.841
"Then again we're only horses.

73
00:04:57.842 --> 00:05:01.332
Who expects us to understand the ways of humans?"

74
00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:03.605
I didn't know the answer to that.

75
00:05:03.606 --> 00:05:14.679
But soon I would learn more about the mysterious ways of humans, when I left that pleasant field behind forever.

